---
title: "announcement_management (kintai-v3: Initial Schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_operation: determine operation type

    q_operation --> q_read: SELECT announcements
    q_operation --> q_write: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE announcements

    q_read --> q_check_auth: evaluate RLS select policy
    q_check_auth --> q_return_data: auth.role() = 'authenticated'
    q_check_auth --> q_deny_read: not authenticated

    q_write --> q_check_admin: evaluate RLS admin policy
    q_check_admin --> q_validate: is_admin() = true
    q_check_admin --> q_deny_write: is_admin() = false

    q_validate --> q_check_current: check is_current constraint
    q_check_current --> q_apply: is_current = false OR no other row has is_current = true
    q_check_current --> q_conflict: another row already has is_current = true

    q_apply --> [*]: operation successful

    q_return_data --> [*]: return announcement rows
    q_deny_read --> [*]: authentication required
    q_deny_write --> [*]: admin role required
    q_conflict --> [*]: unique partial index violation on is_current

    note right of q_check_auth
        INV-001: Any authenticated user can read announcements
        INV-002: Only admins can create, update, or delete announcements
    end note

    note right of q_check_current
        INV-003: At most one announcement can have is_current = true (partial unique index)
        INV-004: To set a new current announcement, the previous must be unset first
        INV-005: Table is published to supabase_realtime for live broadcast
    end note
